cff-version: 1.1.0
message: "If you use or build upon Oblivious Compute, please cite this software."
title: "Oblivious Compute"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-23"

authors:
  - family-names: "Fritz"
    given-names: "Denton Paul"

abstract: >-
  Oblivious Compute is a distributed computation model in which independently
  maintained states are projected into a shared medium and evaluated locally
  for admissibility. The designated computational object is the evolving
  relation among those independently maintained states.

keywords:
  - distributed computing
  - models of computation
  - distributed systems
  - admissibility
  - relational computation
  - coordination

license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ObliviousCompute/ObliviousCompute"
